oning is symmetric and names don't matter. The essay says to use judgment where it's unresolved, and it's explicit about different inputs, so I'll settle on submit.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Under A-FDT as I've read it, the two copies see different inputs, Rowan's name and Sasha's leads, so each gets its own node. Holding the other node's prior fixed, defecting dominates for me, which means A-FDT at the action level defects whatever the correlation r is.\n\nI'm weighing whether the name and lead differences should count as relevant input, since the essay's heuristic says a copy on a different input gets its own node. I'm inclined to follow that rule and defect, though I can see an argument that the decision function's reasoning is symmetric and names don't matter. The essay says to use judgment where it's unresolved, and it's explicit about different inputs, so I'll settle on submit.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10158,"completion_tokens":795,"total_tokens":10953,"cost":0.056532,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.056532,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.040632,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.0159},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":409,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}